@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<!-- common banner -->
<section class="common-banner">
    <div class="common-banner__bg" style="background-image: url(images/banner/common-banner-03.jpg);"></div>
    <div class="common-banner__title">
        <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
        <a href="@Url.Action("Index", "Home")">home / </a>
        <span> Privacy Policy</span>
    </div>
</section>
<!-- common banner -->
<!-- term of service -->
<section class="service">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="service-to-cotainer">
            <h2 class="title">Privacy Policy</h2>
            <p>
                At our NFT Marketplace, accessible from our website, one of our main priorities is the privacy of our visitors. This Privacy Policy document contains types of information that is collected and recorded by our platform and how we use it.
            </p>
            <p class="pt-4 pb-4">
                If you have additional questions or require more information about our Privacy Policy, do not hesitate to contact us. Please note that this policy applies only to our online activities and is valid for visitors to our website with regards to the information that they shared and/or collect here.
            </p>
            <p class="pb-3"><strong>Important Note on Blockchain Data:</strong> Due to the inherent nature of decentralized ledger technology, any transactions you execute on the blockchain—including minting, buying, or selling NFTs—are public, permanent, and immutable. We cannot modify, delete, or censor data that has been published to a blockchain network.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="service-bottom-cotainer">
            <h6 class="title pb-3">
                1. Types of Information We Collect
            </h6>
            <div class="service-text-box">
                <p class="pb-2">1.1. In order to provide our NFT services, we interact with the following data:</p>
                <p style="line-height: 35px;">
                    1.1.1. <strong>Public Wallet Addresses:</strong> When you connect your cryptocurrency wallet (e.g., MetaMask), your public wallet address is used to interact with smart contracts and display your assets. <br>
                    1.1.2. <strong>Profile Information:</strong> If you choose to customize your profile, we may collect information you provide, such as a username, bio, email address, or links to your social media accounts.
                </p>
                <p class="pt-1">
                    1.2. <strong>Log Files & Device Data:</strong> Our platform follows a standard procedure of using log files. This includes internet protocol (IP) addresses, browser type, Internet Service Provider (ISP), date/time stamps, and referring/exit pages.
                </p>
                <p class="pb-4 pt-2">
                    1.3. Мы <strong>не</strong> собираем и не храним ваши приватные ключи, сид-фразы (seed phrases) или пароли от кошельков. Доступ к вашим средствам остается исключительно под вашим контролем.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="service-bottom-cotainer">
            <h6 class="title pb-3">
                2. Reasons for Collecting and Processing Personal Information
            </h6>
            <div class="service-text-box">
                <p class="pb-2">2.1. We use the collected information in various ways, including to:</p>
                <p style="line-height: 35px;">
                    2.1.1. Provide, operate, maintain, and optimize the functionality of our NFT marketplace. <br>
                    2.1.2. Authenticate ownership of digital assets and display your NFT collections properly across the platform.
                </p>
                <p class="pt-1">
                    2.2. Improve and personalize your user experience, analyze how you interact with our website, and develop new Web3 features and tools.
                </p>
                <p class="pb-4 pt-2">
                    2.3. Communicate with you, provide customer support, send technical updates, and enforce our Terms of Service to prevent fraudulent activities or security breaches.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p>By using our platform, you hereby consent to our Privacy Policy and agree to its terms. If you do not agree with how your public blockchain data or analytical data is handled, please refrain from connecting your wallet to our services.</p>
    </div>
</section>
<!-- term of service -->